(C) Average abundances (gray dots) of a one-dimensional system with positive feedback in its production given by Eq.~\ref{EQ: OneDSysDef} with rate constants $\beta=1,c=0.1,K=50,n=4$. The linear response coefficient of the stochastic system (solid tangent lines) differs drastically from deterministic sensitivity analyses (dashed lines) when the probability distribution is bimodal. 
Both deterministic response predictions are accurate approximations when the stochastic stationary state distribution is unimodal.
}
\label{FIG: Stochastic Linear Response}
   \vspace{-1em}
