with an invariant $g(y,z,t)=0$. The function $h(y,z,t)$ is defined by \cref{eq:index_1_zdot} if the DAE is of index-1.  For index-2 the invariants are \cref{eq:index_2_dae_alg}, \cref{eq:hidden_constraint}, and the function $h(y,z,t)$ is defined by \cref{eq:zdot_for_index_2}.
Note that the solution $[y, \, z]^T$ of \cref{eq:dae_equation} and \cref{eq:ode_reduced_form} is the same.
