    \caption{The conformal potential $\bar V_{\ell} ( \sigma )$ develops strong gradients in around the horizons as $\eta \rightarrow 0$. In the Schwarzschild scenario (left panel), the strong gradient develop around the cosmological horizon as  $\sigma_\Lambda$ approaches future null infinity. In the de Sitter scenario, it develops around the event horizon as $\sigma_h$ approaches the singularity. The inset figures show the rate of convergence of the corresponding Chebyshev coefficients representing $\bar V_{\ell} ( \sigma )$ without AnMR. As $\eta \rightarrow 0$, the strong gradient near the horizons yields a loss of accuracy, which forces one to allocate much more computing power to get a proper accuracy for a QNM solver. }
