\subsection{TrendFolios\textregistered{}  Equity Strategy}

The TrendFolios\textregistered{} Equity Strategy implements momentum and trend-following methodology across equity ETFs representing various risk factors including valuation (growth vs. value), market capitalization (large vs. small), and geographic exposure (U.S., developed international, and emerging markets). This systematic approach uses a proprietary algorithm that combines quantitative momentum signals with technical trend-following indicators to determine portfolio inclusion or exclusion. The strategy employs tracking error measurements rather than standard deviation for its inverse volatility weighting scheme, allocating more capital to factors with lower tracking error and less capital to those with higher tracking error. This construction method aims to ensure each equity factor contributes approximately equal relative risk to the overall portfolio while capturing trending risk factors within the equity universe.

