\noindent {\bf Commodities} 

Commodities are traded on futures exchanges, which is another jurisdiction than stocks and contains different participants. ETFs and other legal changes are making this space more accessible. Commodities involve the ownership of raw materials and physical goods such as metals, oil, natural gas, and agricultural products traded in futures markets. Instead of providing capital to entrepreneurs, the investment is in the natural resources provided by the earth and prices are determined by supply and demand.

Key characteristics include:

