\label{sec:bg}

% Define the problem we are trying to solve
% We first define state, trajectory, and interval before introducing the problem statement.
Let a trajectory (or a signal) of $n$-dimensional states be a discrete-time series $\tau = s_0, s_1, \dots, s_H$, where $s_t \in S$ is a state at timestep $t \in \mathbb{Z}_{>0}$, $S \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n$ is the state space, and $H$ is the time horizon of $\tau$. 
We also define an interval $I$ as $I:=[a,b] = \{k \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq0} | a\leq k \leq b; a,b\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq0}\}$, $\abs{I}$ as the cardinality of $I$, and $t+I$ as the interval $[t+a, t+b]$.

