metrics for evaluating preference over a generic HRTF are commonly grouped into three dimensions: \emph{coloration}, \emph{externalization}, and \emph{localization}~\cite{majdak2013sound, brinkmann2017authenticity, jenny2020usability}. However, it is still unclear whether these perceptual dimensions are captured in existing representation learning methods, and how to further align the learned latent representations with perception beyond these baselines.  

