\end{equation}
where $A$ is the set of latent space distances and $B$ is the set of perceptual metric values (e.g., PBC) between the HRTFs. For subjects $i, j \in \{1, 2, \dots, N\}$, we compute $L_2$ distance in the latent space as $\| \mathbf{z}_i - \mathbf{z}_j \|_2$, as $L_2$ distance is effective for capturing the geometric structure of data that is normally distributed or approximately so. The distance in the perceptual metrics space is $m_{i,j} = f(\mathbf{x}_i, \mathbf{x}_j)$, where $f$ is any of the computational auditory models introduced in Section~\ref{ssec:perceptualMetrics}.
