\section{Aligning with Perception-Informed Space}

We design our methods using the PBC metric as an example and further evaluate its generalization ability in Section~\ref{ssec:generalize}. For representation learning, we use the INR model~\cite{zhang2023hrtf}, which originally employs implicit gradient-based optimization~\cite{bond2020gradient} to simultaneously learn the latent representation and the generative model. To incorporate constraints into the latent space during training, we adapt the training paradigm to generative latent optimization~\cite{bojanowski18glo}, which was also applied in~\cite{lobato2024process}. In this modified approach, the latent space for each training subject is randomly initialized and then optimized jointly with the model weights to find the best latent variables for each sample. During inference, we treat the optimization as an inverse problem, similar to GAN inversion~\cite{9792208}, where we optimize the latent vectors by minimizing the loss while keeping the model weights fixed.

