		\end{tikzcd}
	\end{equation}
\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}
	We have to check that~$\eta$ and~$\epsilon$ satisfy zigzag identities. 
	This is straightforward because~$\eta$ only consists of identity morphisms. 
	By \Cref{lem:identification of relative tensor products of morphisms} below, $\gamma_{ F(X,u)}^{g,h,k}$ and therefore $\epsilon_{ F(X,u)}$ also reduce to identities, and we obtain $\epsilon F\circ  F\eta=\id_ F$. 
	Similarly, by \eqref{eq:compatibility of gamma with group multiplication} we have $\gamma^{g,e,h}=\gamma^{g,e,e}\circ\gamma^{g,e,h}$, and hence $\gamma_{(Y,\tau)}^{g,e,e}=\id_{Y_{g,e}}$. 
