Additionally, $ \left( \Phi_{s,t} \ ; \ s \leq t < T \right)$ is well defined and satisfies 
for all $(s,x)\in [0,T)\times \R^2$
      \begin{align*}%\label{eq:limphi}
      \Phi_{s,T}(x):= \lim_{t\uparrow T} \Phi_{s,t}(x)=\Phi(x)
   \end{align*}
   and
$t \mapsto k_t$ satisfies the identity 
