\end{talign}
where ``$\Rightarrow$'' means ``imply''. Next, we leverage two new auxiliary variables $T^{(u)}_n$ and $T^{(s)}_{n,m}$ to replace the delay in Equations (\text{\ref{eq.cost_u2}}) and (\text{\ref{eq.cost_s2}}). With the introduction of these two variables, there would be four more new constraints:
