\section{Conclusions}
We have shown that a version of {\sc reduce} from more than 50 years ago can be built and run today, and that it was already highly capable.
We have detailed the process of getting it running on a minimal Lisp and have seen that doing so recalls all the Lisp portability issues from that era. 
The resulting system is tiny by today's standards
and requires no more resources than those of current microcontrollers. % see ulisp.com

