\noindent \textbf{Setting profit-maximizing prices under the naive model}

We first consider the scenario where the retailer uses the naive demand model to set uniform offline prices for each category. The retailer then maximizes expected profit per person, defined as:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{eq:naive.profit.function}
 %   \tilde{R}(\mathbf{p}) & = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} \sum_{j=1}^{J}(p_{j} - m_{j})\times \frac{\exp(\tilde{\psi}_{ij})}{1 + \sum_{j'=1}^{J} \exp(\tilde{\psi}_{ij'})} = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} \tilde{R}_{i}(\mathbf{p})
\tilde{R}(\mathbf{p}) & = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} \sum_{j=1}^{J}(p_{j} - m_{j})\times \tilde{Pr}_{ij}(\mathbf{p}) = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} \tilde{R}_{i}(\mathbf{p})
