\end{defnitalic}

By solving the system of $J$ equations defined in \eqref{eq:naive.model.j_th_FOC}, we can numerically solve for the uniform price vectors under the naive model. This solution serves as a benchmark for evaluating the profit implications of accounting for the online adoption effect under uniform pricing. 

\noindent \textbf{Setting profit-maximizing prices under our model}

Then, we consider the scenario in which the retailer uses our model, accounting for the online adoption effect, to set uniform offline prices. The retailer maximizes the expected profit per customer given by: 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\label{eq:uniform.profit.function}
 %   R(\mathbf{p}) & = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} \sum_{j=1}^{J}(p_{j} - m_{j})\times \frac{\exp(\psi_{ij})}{1 + \sum_{j'=1}^{J} \exp(\psi_{ij'})} = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} R_{i}(\mathbf{p})
