\subsubsection{ Niederreiter Framework}
The Niederreiter framework \cite{niederreiter1986knapsack} uses the parity-check matrix instead of the generator matrix, resulting in an equivalently secure system. Niederreiter originally proposed using GRS codes as secret codes. In this scheme the plaintext is encoded as a vector of length $n$ and weight less than or equal to the error correcting capacity of the code. The general Niederreiter framework with a linear code is presented in Table ~\ref{tab:niederreiter}.
