\hline
\textbf{Key Sizes} & Large (e.g., McEliece keys: $\approx$1 MB--1 GB due to matrix-based structures). Recent code-based FHE schemes still struggle with key size reduction. & Smaller (e.g., Ring-LWE keys: $\approx$ 1-10 KB). Optimizations like NTT (Number Theoretic Transform) enable compact representations. \\
\hline
\textbf{Computation Speed} & Matrix/vector operations are parallelizable but computationally heavy. Simpler arithmetic (e.g., XOR-based operations in some schemes). & Faster due to polynomial ring optimizations (e.g., NTT accelerates multiplication in CKKS/BGV \cite{cheon2017homomorphic}). \\
\hline
