Then there is a unique $2$-cell $g:\left( f,\mathcal{F}\right)
\Rightarrow \left( f^{\prime },\mathcal{F}^{\prime }\right) $ such that $%
\left( \id\otimes\varepsilon,1\otimes 1\right) g=g_{1}$ and $\left( \varepsilon\otimes\id,1\otimes 1\right)
g=g_{2},$ explicitly given by $g=(\id\ot\varepsilon\ot\varepsilon\ot\id)((\Ff')^{-1})(g_1\otimes g_2)(\id\ot\varepsilon\ot\varepsilon\ot\id)(\Ff)$. 
